id: pm-2irc1p
title: "GH-865: classify linked-test lock contention as infrastructure collision"
description: Linked tests that fail because another process holds a tool or filesystem lock are currently classified as assertion_failure. Recognize narrow lock-acquisition timeout and already-running evidence as retryable infra_collision without weakening real assertion classification.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:sdk","area:testing",classification,github-report,linked-tests,reliability
created_at: "2026-08-02T06:47:21.892Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T11:35:47.576Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#b54ea3df17a9d4f6f64078c0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Narrow lock-contention stderr is classified as infra_collision through SDK and CLI paths; Unrelated lock words and genuine assertion failures remain assertion_failure; The GitHub report is linked to this canonical PM item
goal: project management = context management
objective: Verification evidence distinguishes retryable environment contention from product defects
value: Agents can retry infrastructure collisions instead of debugging false product failures
impact: Makes linked-test evidence truthful and reduces wasted investigation
outcome: Identical commands that pass after a competing lock clears are reported as retryable infrastructure collisions
why_now: GitHub #865 reproduced the mismatch on the current 2026.8.2 release
parent: pm-92if
risk: low
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub #865
severity: medium
expected_result: Lock acquisition contention is infra_collision
actual_result: Lock acquisition contention is assertion_failure
affected_version: 2026.8.2
component: linked-test SDK/CLI classification
regression: true
